# ============================================
# ET:LEGACY DISCORD BOT - GITIGNORE v2.0
# ============================================
# Philosophy: Track source code, config templates, docs, CI.
# Never track: secrets, backups, logs, generated outputs, dev scratch files.
# Files already tracked need: git rm --cached <file>
# ============================================

# ============================================
# ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS (NEVER COMMIT)
# ============================================
.env
# Secret backup copies (audit AUD-010): deploys/ops sometimes drop a dated
# .env backup in the checkout — never let one be committed. Real backups live
# in a root-only location outside the repo with a documented retention policy.
.env.bak
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak
*.env.bak
# The documented rotation naming is .env.backup.YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS (see
# docs/SECRETS_MANAGEMENT.md); the generic *.backup rule below does NOT catch
# the timestamp suffix, so ignore .env.backup* explicitly (Codex review #514).
.env.backup
.env.backup*
.prodenv
.envcopy
.db_credentials
.redis_credentials
.ssh/
*.pem
*.key

# ============================================
# PYTHON
# ============================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ============================================
# NODE / REACT
# ============================================
node_modules/
# ⚠️ Without the slash too: a worktree that shares the dev tree's packages does
# it with a SYMLINK, and `node_modules/` matches directories only — so the link
# showed up as untracked and one `git add -A` away from committing a pointer
# into someone's home directory.
node_modules
website/frontend/test-results/
website/frontend/playwright-report/
gemini-website/dist/
gemini-website/.next/
build/
website/static/modern/
website/static/app/
# corpus recorder output — phase tests commit chosen fixtures as copies
tests/fixtures/api/recorded/
# Deploy staging/rollback dirs for the modern build (deploy_release.sh step 3c).
# MUST be ignored: the deploy's clean-tree guard aborts on any untracked path,
# so an un-ignored static/modern.prev left after a deploy would break the next one.
website/static/modern.new/
website/static/modern.prev/

